2. Definitions

"You" means the individual or organization exercising these permissions.
"Authorized Users" are you and members of a defined private group whom you
authorize for a personal, educational, testing or internal purpose, such as
your household, enrolled class or work team. A group open to anyone who signs
up, pays or follows a public invitation is public.

"Private Use" means use by Authorized Users alone for one of those purposes.
"Substantial Functionality" means a core capability of the Covered Material,
such as assembling, running or debugging 8086 programs, even when accessed
through a different interface or as part of a larger product.

"Public Hosting" means operating a publicly accessible copy of the Covered
Material, or providing the general public with network access to Substantial
Functionality implemented by it. This includes websites, online applications,
embedded emulators and APIs, whether free or paid.

3. Permissions

Subject to this license, anyone may view, study and download the source.
You have a worldwide, nonexclusive, royalty-free license to run the software
locally and to copy, build, modify and self-host it for Private Use. You may
make backups and provide Authorized Users with the source or built copies
they need for that use. Keep those copies within the group and provide this
license with them. No separate permission or payment is required.

Private self-hosting includes localhost, a restricted LAN, a personal server,
and a VPN or authenticated internet service. An internet-connected server
qualifies if access to the software and its functionality is restricted to
Authorized Users and the service is not offered to the public.

4. GitHub and contributions

You may use GitHub's repository features to view and fork the public source
and submit changes to the project by pull request. This license preserves
the rights granted under GitHub's applicable platform terms. Serving a working
public emulator from a fork, including through GitHub Pages, requires prior
written permission under section 5.

For your own original contributions submitted by pull request, you retain
ownership and grant Sergiu Lefter a nonexclusive, royalty-free license to
use and modify them, host them in the official emulator, and include them in
project versions distributed under this license. Identify any third-party
material you submit and its terms. You can grant only rights you control.

